  "articleBody": "Fixing drywall damage properly takes more than just spreading compound over a hole. If you have damaged sheetrock from plumbing repairs, door impacts, or settling, understanding what a quality repair requires will help you choose the right contractor.\n\nKey Benefits of Full-Scope Patching\nA proper patch restores the structural integrity of your wall, prevents hairline cracks along repair seams, and creates an even surface that blends into your existing wall texture.\n\nProcess Breakdown\nFirst, your contractor inspects the opening and squares off broken edges. Small holes may need mesh backing, while larger openings require solid backing wood and fitted drywall that matches existing sheetrock thickness. Next, joints are taped, followed by thin coats of joint compound feathered outward. Each coat must dry completely before sanding and applying wall primer.\n\nReal Examples\nA pipe leak repair often leaves an open stud bay. Simply covering it with a surface patch leaves a weak spot; a professional installs solid framing backing and seals joints to prevent sagging.\n\nWhat Can Change the Right Choice\nThe location, wall texture, and nearby utilities dictate the scope. Ceiling patches or repairs near wiring demand specialized care. For expert repairs across the Denver area, contact Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC by calling 303-505-0866.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
